    <!-- Special Notes -->
    <special_notes>
        <note category="gender_suffix">
            All products use same base product ID for both men's and ladies' versions (no M/L suffix in product ID)
        </note>
        <note category="sizing">
            Width is fixed per product ID - cannot be customized
        </note>
        <note category="customization">
            Custom engraving available on interior of all bands
        </note>
        <note category="heritage">
            Roman key pattern dates to ancient Greece and Rome (800 BC - 400 AD)
            Jelling band pattern from Viking Age Denmark (10th century AD)
            Greek key variant represents additional Hellenic design traditions
            Runic script from Norse/Viking culture (2nd-8th centuries AD)
            Byzantine cross from Eastern Roman Empire (330-1453 AD)
            Celtic patterns represent Irish/Scottish/Welsh cultural heritage adapted for cultural collection
        </note>
        <note category="cultural_appeal">
            These patterns appeal to customers seeking heritage designs from multiple cultures:
            Greek/Roman classical traditions, Norse/Viking heritage, Byzantine religious symbolism,
            and Celtic cultural interpretations distinct from the main Celtic collection
        </note>
    </special_notes>
